WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:02.780
What would television be without Netflix?

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.620
Wait, stop — it's too unbearable to even
imagine.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:11.040
Netflix's introduction of show after awesome
show in 2016 left TV watchers hardly able

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.000
to catch their breaths, and it doesn't look
like Netflix is going to slow down in 2017.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.390
With a miles-long list of series to binge-watch
in the coming months, here are the Netflix

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:23.710
shows that will blow everyone away in 2017.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.710
Frontier

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:30.429
Frontier premiered on Discovery Channel Canada
in November 2016 to some seriously solid ratings,

00:00:30.429 --> 00:00:35.690
and made the move to Netflix mid-January 2017,
giving TV lovers the perfect excuse to watch

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:37.769
all six episodes in a single sitting.

00:00:37.769 --> 00:00:42.570
This Canadian-American period drama chronicles
a band of men battling to reclaim ownership

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.999
and seize control of the fur trade in 18th-century
North America, and there's one familiar face

00:00:47.999 --> 00:00:49.730
that may very well have fans cheering.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.510
Game of Thrones' Jason Momoa, better known
as the beloved Khal Drogo, is back on the

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.929
not-so-big screen!

00:00:55.929 --> 00:01:00.430
Frontier is a multi-perspective series that
weaves through cultural relations and the

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.010
savagery of America in its adolescence.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:08.360
Not only does the show promise a healthy portion
of violence, insane action sequences, and

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.430
sharp dialogue, but it also presents a historical
glimpse into the preindustrial times in North

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:14.430
America.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.430
Education and entertainment?

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.110
That's a win-win.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.659
Santa Clarita Diet

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:23.119
Sheila and Joel Hammond may seem like a normal
suburban pair of real estate agents, but their

00:01:23.119 --> 00:01:24.689
fridge tells another story.

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:28.360
If you love zombie stories, but you're looking
for relief from the constant misery of The

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.310
Walking Dead, be sure to check out the comedy-horror
series Santa Clarita Diet, which premiered

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.380
on Netflix in early February.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.960
Starring Drew Barrymore and Timothy Olyphant
as a California couple, Santa Clarita Diet

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.909
follows Sheila's radical transformation, who
may end up biting off more than she can chew

00:01:44.909 --> 00:01:45.909
— literally.

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:46.909
Mindhunter

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:52.450
Based on the book of the same name, this Netflix
series rolls time back to 1979 with Jonathan

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:58.299
Groff and Holt McCallany starring as FBI Behavioral
Science Unit special agents who take on the

00:01:58.299 --> 00:02:02.690
daunting task of conducting interviews with
currently imprisoned criminals.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:06.689
But not just any criminals: these two sit
eye-to-eye with serial killers.

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:11.590
With Charlize Theron and David Fincher in
Mind Hunter's executive producer seats, brace

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.520
yourself for a drama that will leave you sleeping
with the lights on.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.590
Marvel's Iron Fist

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:21.650
Superhero films, series, and spinoffs are
huge hits with audiences worldwide.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.220
Recently, Netflix rolled out a triple threat
of comic crime-fighting shows in Marvel's

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.830
Jessica Jones, Luke Cage, and Daredevil.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:33.360
In 2017, Netflix is adding yet another superhero
show to its stable: Marvel's Iron Fist.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.690
The fourth Marvel series to find its home
on Netflix, Iron Fist stars Finn Jones in

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.690
the title role.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:42.940
Billionaire Buddhist monk Danny Rand has returned
to his home city of New York after spending

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.920
years as a recluse, honing his unparalleled
martial arts prowess.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.380
Danny summons the power of — you guessed
it — the Iron Fist, as he takes down New

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.540
York's most corrupt villains with a deadly
punch.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:59.590
The series hits Netflix in full on March 17,
2017, and helps set the stage for...

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:00.670
Marvel's The Defenders

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:04.300
Though an official release date has yet to
be announced, Marvel's The Defenders will

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.760
definitely be buzzed about right up until
it reaches screens, and likely well beyond.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.450
The eight-episode miniseries brings together
all of those heroes audiences know and love

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:18.430
from their standalone shows: Krysten Ritter
as Jessica Jones; Mike Colter as Luke Cage;

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:23.290
Charlie Cox as Daredevil; and the guy we just
talked about, Finn Jones as Iron Fist.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:28.230
Also joining the superhero-studded character
ensemble are Elektra Natchios, vigilante nurse

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:32.510
Claire Temple, and the sophisticated and sinister
villain, Alexandra.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.860
The group takes on all the bad guys in mid-2017.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.310
Bill Nye Saves the World

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.850
If you were American and in school during
the '90s and early '00s, you likely remember

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:47.360
the notoriously catchy theme song to the live-action
educational science show, Bill Nye the Science

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:47.860
Guy.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.182
"Bill Nye The Science Guy!"

00:03:49.682 --> 00:03:55.310
The famed science educator and mechanical
engineer who taught viewers about cells, photosynthesis,

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.810
and the mysteries of the night sky is back
— this time for his very own talk show.

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:04.290
Bill Nye Saves the World will go beyond the
realm of just science, extending into politics,

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.200
fiscal and social trends, and pop culture
phenomena across the globe.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.620
With a lot of interesting ground to cover,
Nye calls in backup with a few special field

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:17.189
correspondents, so audiences can learn about
the wonders of the world and its people, places,

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:23.289
and things as Mr. Nye debunks myths and refutes
anti-science claims in spring 2017.

00:04:23.289 --> 00:04:25.710
Wet Hot American Summer: Ten Years Later

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:31.629
Despite being a box-office bust, 2001's Wet
Hot American Summer was a cult-favorite comedy,

00:04:31.629 --> 00:04:37.069
with a talented cast that included Molly Shannon,
Paul Rudd, Elizabeth Banks, Michael Ian Black,

00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:40.330
Bradley Cooper, and Amy Poehler, just to name
a few.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:44.940
Nearly a decade and a half later, fans still
wanted more, so Netflix released an eight-episode

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.590
prequel series in the summer of 2015, which
was ridiculous in the best way possible: all

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:54.280
the actors reprised their roles, only to play
even younger versions of their beloved characters.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:59.120
Next comes Wet Hot American Summer: Ten Years
Later, in which the cast collaborates once

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.530
again, this time at a more age-appropriate
level.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:06.860
The sequel series is set in 1991 and is inspired
by some classic '80s comedies.

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:07.860
Friends from College

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:12.139
Starring one of the funniest funny men out
there, Keegan-Michael Key, alongside How I

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:16.220
Met Your Mother's Cobie Smulders, Friends
from College's premise is one that becomes

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:19.940
reality for almost everyone: you and your
once-rowdy college friends are officially

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:24.110
middle-aged — and you're coping with it
in some pretty interesting ways.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.320
"Sorry, sorry.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.200
We're going streaking!"

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:31.210
Dark

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:35.340
We all know how captivated audiences were
in the summer of 2015 when Making a Murderer

00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:40.090
made its Netflix debut, subsequently taking
the TV-watching world by storm with its winding

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:43.699
tale of drama, behind-the-scenes footage,
and shocking secrets.

00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:48.650
It seems history will repeat itself with Dark,
a family drama that tracks the trauma and

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:53.069
devastation that rock a small German town
following the mysterious disappearance of

00:05:53.069 --> 00:05:54.069
two children.

00:05:54.069 --> 00:05:57.860
While it's a work of fiction, it seems the
show is guaranteed to incite goosebumps and

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.010
grim realizations in its audience throughout
its 10-episode first season.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.010
Big Mouth

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:06.580
It's not all going to be gritty thrillers
and action-filled shows coming to Netflix

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:07.810
in 2017.

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:12.779
This tongue-in-cheek, slightly risky animated
comedy from Nick Kroll and Andrew Goldberg

00:06:12.779 --> 00:06:17.120
has been a long time coming: as Kroll put
it in a Netflix press release, "Andrew and

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:21.699
I have been best friends since first grade,
so this show is over 30 years in the making."

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:27.229
Not only does Kroll serve as creator, he's
also voicing one of the main characters: himself.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:28.229
Girlboss

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:33.979
Sophia Amoruso's acclaimed autobiography Girlboss
is getting the Netflix adaptation treatment

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:38.669
in a series centered around the clothing brand
entrepreneur's rise to success.

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:43.770
Starting off humbly selling vintage threads
on eBay, Amoruso shot into international stardom

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:49.910
after starting up the wildly popular and wickedly
trendy fashion-brand-turned-empire Nasty Gal,

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:55.490
and this comedy series will explore her story
with its 13 episode debut in April.

00:06:55.490 --> 00:06:56.490
Ozark

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:01.180
Filmgoers saw Jason Bateman play a slightly
more sinister character than his usual goofball

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.870
charmer in Joel Edgerton's 2015 thriller The
Gift.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:11.169
Now, Bateman's settling into another sordid
role in Netflix's upcoming series Ozark.

00:07:11.169 --> 00:07:15.669
Bateman stars as a financial planner who packs
up his life in the Chicago suburbs and heads

00:07:15.669 --> 00:07:18.800
to a home near the Lake of the Ozarks in Missouri.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.969
But his intentions aren't so squeaky clean...

00:07:21.969 --> 00:07:23.470
Stranger Things 2

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:27.350
Following up on their breakout first season,
the Duffer Brothers will return to Hawkins,

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.879
Indiana for some more monstrous throwback
fun with Stranger Things 2, which debuts on

00:07:31.879 --> 00:07:32.879
Halloween.

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:36.499
The second season of Stranger Things will
pick up a year after the first season left

00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:41.460
off, after its crew of kid adventurers defeated
the Demogorgon — but lost contact with their

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:43.090
friend Eleven in the process.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:47.471
If the Super Bowl previews for Stranger Things
2 are any indication, the intensity of the

00:07:47.471 --> 00:07:52.169
show's second season is going to be full-tilt,
and fans will be tempted to ditch out on the

00:07:52.169 --> 00:07:56.939
usual trick-or-treat routine for an evening
spent watching every episode of the new season.

00:07:56.939 --> 00:08:01.749
Count on Stranger Things 2 to be even, well,
stranger than the first season, with a storm

00:08:01.749 --> 00:08:06.189
coming along to bring some new otherworldly
baddies into the small town fold.

00:08:06.189 --> 00:08:07.189
Dear White People

00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:12.559
2014 saw the indie film Dear White People
bring racial tensions in a bright-white community

00:08:12.559 --> 00:08:16.280
to the surface, and handled it with a ton
of smarts and satire.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:20.640
Piggybacking on the original film comes the
television adaptation of the same name, with

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:25.460
a group of Ivy League students of color navigating
their nearly all-white Winchester University

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.919
campus to discover not only is the lack of
diversity shocking, but so is the number of

00:08:29.919 --> 00:08:32.940
misinformed or just plain biased students.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:33.940
El Chapo

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:38.330
Netflix seems to have kept its eye on the
foreign entertainment realm heading into 2017,

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:42.370
as the company has teamed up with Spanish
language broadcast network Univision for this

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:47.460
upcoming drama series centered around real-life
drug lord and wanted criminal Joaquín Archivaldo

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:51.330
Guzmán Loera, more commonly known by his
nickname, "El Chapo."

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:56.100
The drama series, based on the trials and
insane illegal endeavors of Guzmán's life,

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.081
will hit UniMas audiences before it reaches
Netflix subscribers, but when it does, it

00:09:01.081 --> 00:09:02.950
promises to deliver big time.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:04.120
Thanks for watching!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.830
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:09.030
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

